      "content": "While a company must prioritize financial stability, modern leadership theory increasingly views treating layoffs as a permanent solution as a distraction that devalues the long-term opportunity to upgrade existing assets. If redundant staff can be retrained to fill new roles generated by AI, it is often financially superior to invest in their transition rather than paying the sunk costs associated with recruitment and onboarding new hires later. Therefore, optimizing your workforce isn't just about cutting headcount, but strategically reallocating human capital to where it adds the most value without sacrificing your core mission.",
